Yes. After looking across paleontology data, agent-based simulation, multi-agent RL, graph/analytics tooling, and current LTX pipelines, I think the architecture is now fairly clear.

The central object should be **the animal**, not the video.

Everything downstream—matchups, cards, simulations, scripts, images, fights, arena variants, Shorts—should be generated from a versioned, evidence-backed animal model.

