# 4. Literature pipeline

This is where the simulator becomes substantially better than AI-generated stat cards.

Use:

### OpenAlex

OpenAlex exposes a connected scholarly graph of:

```text
works
authors
sources
institutions
topics
```

and allows searching/filtering over its API. ([OpenAlex][5])

For every animal:

```text
Titanoboa
   ↓
OpenAlex query
   ↓
papers mentioning Titanoboa
   ↓
rank:
    taxonomic description
    biomechanics
    mass estimates
    paleoenvironment
    physiology
```

Then ingest the relevant results.

---

### Crossref

Use Crossref primarily for DOI resolution and authoritative publication metadata; its REST API exposes work metadata and search parameters. ([CrossRef API][6])

---

### Unpaywall / OpenAlex OA

For DOI-bearing papers, use OA discovery to find legally accessible copies. Unpaywall exposes free programmatic DOI lookup, although interestingly its own current guidance recommends using OpenAlex for new integrations where possible because OpenAlex now exposes the broader scholarly metadata ecosystem. ([Unpaywall][7])

So I'd actually do:

```text
OpenAlex
   ↓
DOI
   ↓
OA location
   ↓
paper
```

