# 6. Graph implementation

My recommendation:

```text
CANONICAL STORAGE
PostgreSQL

GRAPH OPERATIONS
NetworkX

BULK ANALYTICS
DuckDB

SIMULATION
Python
```

NetworkX already provides graph creation/manipulation/analysis in Python. ([GitHub][10])

So you can load a subset:

```python
G = graph_for_taxon("Titanoboa")
```

and traverse:

```text
Titanoboa
→ occurrences
→ formations
→ contemporaries
→ environments
→ papers
→ traits
```

No additional server required.

If you eventually have tens of millions of richly traversed graph edges, *then* reconsider a dedicated graph store.

