# 15. Automatically discover interesting battles

This is one of the coolest parts.

After simulation, calculate:

```text
CONTENT SCORE =
surprise
× closeness
× variance
× scientific-interest
× visual-interest
```

Examples:

### Boring

```text
A wins 99.9%
same outcome everywhere
```

Probably skip it.

### Great episode

```text
A wins 51%
B wins 49%

BUT

swamp:
A = 81%

open terrain:
B = 76%
```

Automatic title candidate:

> **One Change Completely Reverses This Prehistoric Fight**

The simulator discovers the story.

