# The real moat

It's not the simulator algorithm.

It's this:

```text
               SOURCED ANIMAL
                     │
             uncertainty model
                     │
              visual identity
                     │
              behavior model
                     │
              simulation history
                     │
                media history
                     │
                 audience data
```

After 500 animals and 1,000 videos, you have a **machine-readable prehistoric world**.

Then the same Titanoboa object powers:

```text
species page
historical map
Top-Trumps card
size comparison
1v1 fight
team fight
documentary
arena experiment
quiz
interactive simulator
game
```

That's why I'd build the **animal graph first** and let content be a projection of it.

And the same architecture later works for historical armies, ships, mythic entities, ancient cities, or basically any domain where you can construct evidence-backed entities and place them into counterfactual scenarios.

